{
  "_about": "The mentors of the tasks (src/core/mentor.js; docs/MENTOR.md). The person who gives a task watches the child, reads the error, and chooses one move after each commit, and on idle time. mastery: at this P(L) the person only watches. ready: P(L) over this, with fast right commits, is ready for more. top: the highest help level. handover: the self-corrections of the child after which the person first waits before a mark (the first number), and then only watches (the second). families: how a family of tasks reads its commits. reader: sum (the sum of the parts against the target), each (each part against the target: the kinds of the basket), or plain (only right or not). slip: an error of at most this many units is a slip. fastPart: seconds for each part; a try faster than this is fast. slowUnit: seconds for each unit of the target; a right try slower than this is counting all. idleStart: seconds with no action at the start of a task (does not know what to do). offerAfter: seconds of idle time after a miss, with no wave, before the person offers help. look: the seconds that the person waits after a miss for the child to look first (the second stage of the handover). frustrated: misses in a row; bored: fast clean commits in a row (the same number, so that boredom gets a response as soon as frustration). ladders: for each diagnosis, the moves in the order of the help level. mentors: the mentor of each task (the task id of its skill events): its family, its person (the entity that acts), demo (the look of the other instance of a demonstration: its prop, and the look of its things; size is the size of a thing), and picture (the line that sends the child to another station). lines: the line of each move (the person says it in a bubble). again: the line of a move that helped this child before (the person says it as information).",
